  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/assets/9df3b88fb441956592ef8c45214c4728bb321f6fd6b627eb67ce3ce963438915.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is the path comprising of a vertical line segment of length $5$ and a semicircle of radius $4,$ as  shown above.",
  "worked_solution": "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{2}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${y}_{1}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{1}=4$ and  ${y}_{2}=-1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1}=(-1)-4=-5.\n$$",
